---

## Summary of the call chain

`OwnersApi.addOwner` (generated interface, defines the mapping + `@Valid`) → `OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner` → `OwnerMapper.toOwner` → `CustomerCode.of` → `clinicService.saveOwner` → `SpringDataOwnerRepository.save` → `OwnerMapper.toOwnerDto` (with `@AfterMapping` side effects). Bean validation is triggered by `@Valid` on the DTO, augmented by a custom `@InitBinder` `Validator` (`OwnerFieldsValidationAdvice`) that also mutates the payload (address + telephone normalization). Entity-level constraints also exist on `Owner`/`Person`.

---

## 1. The mapping + `@Valid` (generated interface)

The POST /owners → `addOwner` mapping and request-body validation live in the generated interface, not the controller.

`/home/daniel/sandbox/target/generated-sources/openapi/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/api/OwnersApi.java` lines 52, 79-87:

```java
